A '''multicombat area''', also known as a '''Multiway Combat area''' is an area of the ''[[Old School RuneScape]]'' world where a [[player]] or [[monster]] can be attacked by more than one player or monster at a time.

Multicombat areas are identified upon entering by two crossed swords ([[File:Multicombat.png|This icon indicates that a player is in a multicombat area]]) which appear in the bottom right-hand corner of the [[interface]] or under the mini [[world map]]. Anywhere else is a [[Single-way combat]] area, also known as a single-combat area, with an exception for the [[Revenant Caves]], [[Wilderness Agility Course]] and lesser Wilderness bosses, which are [[Singles-plus combat]] ([[File:Singles plus.png]]).

Multicombat areas are especially dangerous in the [[Wilderness]], as a player can be attacked by more than one monster or player at a time. It is very useful, though, to be in a multicombat area while monster killing monsters with friends, as lone players can be picked off quickly.

While players can enter multi-combat in single combat zones, this only happens if the player isn't under attack by another monster. Examples include barraging a clump of monsters or hiding in a spot where they cannot attack them and allowing a [[dwarf multicannon]] to do the job.

