===Mechanics===
{{Sectstub}}
====Enemies larger than 1 tile====
When targeting large enemies, chinchompas, along with burst and barrage spells will usually centre their 3x3 area based on the target's [[true tile]]. This can lead to players feeling that the AoE effects are not working when a large NPC is directly north or east of another adjactent target.

==Trivia==
*Usually, when fighting a single [[monster]] with other players, the player that applied the most total damage at the end of the battle gets the monster's item/coin drop.
*Players can aggravate multiple enemies by simply attacking all of them without killing them then running to a farther location. The [[aggressive]] monsters will follow the player causing the monsters to pile the player.
*What determines if you are in able to attack someone else is based on the zone they are currently in, which means one could attack multiple targets simultaneously from a [[Single-way combat|single-combat zone]], as long as their opponents are in a multicombat area. This will also mean that only one person can attack you if you are in a single-combat area, with the exception of [[Recoil (disambiguation)|recoil]]-oriented damage (i.e. specific [[Ring of recoil|rings]], [[vengeance]] spells, and [[Dharok the Wretched's equipment|Dharok's Amulet-enhanced set effect]]) reverted back on you when performing multi-hitting attacks against multiple targets (that are in a multicombat area) simultaneously.

